  "id": "002",
  "title": "The Billionaire's Divorce Papers",
  "subtitle": "On my third anniversary, my husband had his assistant FedEx me the divorce papers. Three hours later, my grandmother died and left me two billion dollars.",
  "penName": "Sofia Castellanos",
  "genre": "billionaireRomance",
  "hook": "On the morning of my third wedding anniversary, my husband's assistant hand-delivered a FedEx envelope to my office. I thought it was flowers. It was divorce papers, signed by him, not by me. Three hours later, my grandmother — the one I hadn't spoken to in twelve years — died of an aneurysm in Buenos Aires. She left me two billion dollars and one very specific instruction: finish what I started with the Wolfes. I signed the divorce papers. I quit my job. I went shopping. By the end of the quarter, I owned twelve percent of my husband's company.",
